# Rust build artifacts
/target/
**/*.rs.bk

# Cargo.lock - omis pour les binaires (conservé pour les libs)
# Cargo.lock

# Environnement
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Apollia runtime data (local uniquement)
.apollia/
apollia.toml.local
models/
# The CLI end-to-end seed ships three stub GGUF/GGML files of 4 to 8 KiB, read
# by tests/cli/seed/build-seed.sh. The generic rule above aims at real models of
# several hundred megabytes and caught them by accident, which left the case
# `model list shows 2 seeded gguf` failing in any tree but this one.
!tests/cli/seed/files/models/

# Python virtualenvs and tooling caches
.venv/
.venv-agents/
__pycache__/
*.egg-info/
*.pyc
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
.tox/
.nox/

# Desktop build artifacts - staged by scripts/bundle-cli.sh before Tauri build.
# tauri.conf.json declares `apollia-os*` and `python/**/*` as bundle resources,
# and tauri-build fails the whole workspace when a glob matches nothing. Both
# keep one tracked placeholder so a fresh clone or worktree compiles, the same
# trick runners/README.txt already plays for `runners/**/*`. The `python/*` form
# is required: git refuses to re-include a file whose parent directory is
# excluded, so `python/` alone could not carry the negation below.
crates/apollia-desktop/resources/
crates/apollia-desktop/python/*
!crates/apollia-desktop/python/.gitkeep
crates/apollia-desktop/apollia-os

# Dev-only automation harness output (screenshots + report.json)
/.apollia-automation/

# Playwright run output (browser suites of the desktop UI)
crates/apollia-desktop/ui/test-results/
crates/apollia-desktop/ui/playwright-report/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# Coverage
lcov.info

# Logs
*.log

# Docs
docs/internal/
docs/specs/
docs/target/
docs/backlog/

# Coding-assistant session state and per-project tooling. Working method, not
# product: it describes how the tree is worked on, which nobody needs in order
# to build or use it.
.claude/
CLAUDE.md
# Dossier de démonstration - fichiers locaux non versionnés
demo/

# Python bundle cache (packaging)
/target/python-bundle/

# Staged Python bundle (rebuilt at release build time)
/crates/apollia-desktop/resources/python/*
!/crates/apollia-desktop/resources/python/.placeholder

# SonarQube local scan artifacts.
/.sonar/
/.scannerwork/

# Agents that are not part of the public tree. Their sources of truth live in a
# separate private repository. These patterns are belt-and-suspenders: the
# physical move keeps them off the working tree, the entries below catch
# accidental re-introduction.
/agents/_test_forge/
/agents/archive-worker/
/agents/chart-worker/
/agents/docx-worker/
/agents/pdf-worker/
/agents/veille-ia/
/agents/xlsx-worker/
/agents/sanitize-codebase/
# Client engagement material: business referential, evaluation dataset and
# scored baselines are covered by the engagement, not by this repository's
# licence.
/agents/*-classification/

# Performance measurement campaigns. A measurement harness and its result
# records document how the project is worked on, not how the product is built
# or used, and each record carries absolute model paths, a machine identifier
# and an OS version.
/scripts/model-eval/

# The guard that joined the shooting script to the pages it names. It has no
# input left once the shooting script is out of the tree.
/scripts/check_screenshot_script.py
# Narrative overlay for documentation screenshots. The checked-in seed is a test
# fixture whose exact row counts are asserted; the story the screenshots tell is
# a separate artifact that lives outside this repository.
/tests/cli/seed/overlay/

# Dated architecture decision records and their index. The decisions in force
# are stated in the present tense in docs/site/docs/architecture/08-decisions.md
# and its French mirror; the dated corpus is a working record of how the project
# got there, which is planning rather than product.
/docs/adr/
/docs/Decisions-Log.md

# Public roadmap. Held back until it is stable enough to be a commitment rather
# than a sketch: a roadmap that moves every month costs more trust than it buys.
/ROADMAP.md

# Assistant and browser-automation scratch output.
/.playwright-mcp/
/notes/
/llm.txt

# cargo-mutants configuration. Mutation testing is a development practice, not
# part of building or using the product.
/mutants.toml

# Prebuilt STT runner binaries staged for local desktop dev. Opaque
# executables have no place in a repository that is built from source.
/crates/apollia-desktop/runners/*
!/crates/apollia-desktop/runners/README.txt

# Working documents for in-flight engineering programs, never committed.
# Working notes kept at the repository root: R&D programmes and pre-release test
# scratchpads. They are personal, they carry raw machine paths, and a `git add -A`
# on release day would sweep them into the public history. One rule per family
# rather than one per file, so the next note is covered before it is written.
/RD-*.md
/TMP-*.md

# Figma <-> code provenance for the design system. Internal design bookkeeping:
# it tracks in-flight design work and cites internal planning documents.
/crates/apollia-desktop/ui/figma/MAPPING.md

# Docusaurus adopters documentation site (docs/site). Build-time Node artifacts
# and generated API reference (regenerated from clients/openapi.json at build).
/docs/site/node_modules/
/docs/site/build/
/docs/site/.docusaurus/
/docs/site/docs/reference/api/
sdk/build/

# Throwaway seeded data ecosystem for automation verification (build-seed.sh)
.apollia-seed-home/

# CLI E2E suite report output (regenerated each run)
tests/cli/report/

# Backlog de travail: captures et lots. Voir backlog/README.md pour la raison
# de ne pas le publier avant l'ouverture des contributions.
/backlog/
